    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-003.title": "Canarian quesillo (caramel custard)",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-003.allergen": "Allergens identified from the listed ingredients: egg, milk.\n\nQuesillo contains egg: use a food thermometer to check that the centre reaches at least 71°C. Cool promptly and refrigerate for the stated time; a set appearance does not replace a temperature check.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: verify composition, allergens and traces for the exact items selected once official shop prices and product references are available. Do not claim \"allergen-free\" or \"trace-free\" before product verification.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-003.step.0": "Preheat the oven to 170 °C. Place a flan mould inside a deep baking tray.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-003.step.1": "Heat the sugar and water in a saucepan without stirring until they form amber caramel; carefully pour it into the mould.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-003.step.2": "Beat the eggs with the condensed milk, whole milk and a little lemon zest, trying not to introduce too many bubbles.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-003.step.3": "Pour the mixture over the caramel and cover the mould with aluminium foil.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-003.step.4": "Pour hot water into the baking tray until it reaches about halfway up the mould and bake in a water bath for 50–60 minutes, until the centre has set.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-003.step.5": "Let cool completely, refrigerate for at least 4 hours and unmould by running a thin knife around the edge.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-003.ingredient.0": "sweetened condensed milk",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-003.ingredient.1": "whole milk",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-003.ingredient.2": "eggs",
