    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.title": "Homestyle Valencian paella",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.allergen": "No mandatory allergens were identified in the declared simple ingredients; this does not prove the absence of allergens or traces.\n\nPrevent cross-contamination between raw chicken/rabbit and ready-to-eat foods. Check with a food thermometer that chicken reaches at least 74°C at its centre before serving.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: verify composition, allergens and traces for the exact items selected once official shop prices and product references are available. Do not claim \"allergen-free\" or \"trace-free\" before product verification.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.step.0": "Heat the oil in a wide paella pan and brown the chicken and rabbit, turning them so that all sides colour evenly.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.step.1": "Add the flat green beans, sauté for 4 minutes and stir in the crushed tomato; cook until reduced.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.step.2": "Remove the pan briefly from the heat and stir in the sweet paprika so it does not burn.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.step.3": "Pour in the water, add the saffron and cooked garrofón beans; simmer for about 20 minutes to develop a flavoursome broth. Add the rosemary sprig for the final 5 minutes of simmering, then remove it before adding the rice.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.step.4": "Adjust the salt, spread the rice evenly and cook for 8 minutes over high heat and 10 minutes over medium-low heat without stirring.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.step.5": "Check that the chicken and rabbit are fully cooked, turn off the heat and let rest for 5 minutes before serving.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.ingredient.0": "short-grain rice",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.ingredient.1": "chicken, cut into pieces",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.ingredient.2": "rabbit, cut into pieces",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.ingredient.3": "flat green beans",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.ingredient.4": "cooked garrofón beans (large white lima beans)",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.ingredient.5": "crushed tomato",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.ingredient.6": "olive oil",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.ingredient.7": "sweet paprika",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.ingredient.8": "saffron",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.ingredient.9": "water",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.ingredient.10": "rosemary (sprig)",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.unmeasured.0": "salt",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.unmeasuredNote.0": "to taste",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.editorial.0": "Salt is listed as a seasoning to taste, with no invented numerical amount; excluded from automatic shopping.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.editorial.1": "Rosemary: steep during the final five minutes of the broth and remove before the rice; editorial decision supported by Spain Tourism, absent from the V47 source.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.editorial.2": "Prevent cross-contamination between raw chicken/rabbit and ready-to-eat foods. Check with a food thermometer that chicken reaches at least 74°C at its centre before serving.",
