    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-004.editorial.4": "Rest: 5 min. This is not a total duration.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-005.title": "Andalusian gazpacho",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-005.allergen": "No mandatory allergens were identified in the declared simple ingredients; this does not prove the absence of allergens or traces.\n\nWash all vegetables eaten raw carefully and keep gazpacho refrigerated until serving. Wine vinegar may contain sulphites: check the label of the selected brand.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: verify composition, allergens and traces for the exact items selected once official shop prices and product references are available. Do not claim \"allergen-free\" or \"trace-free\" before product verification.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-005.step.0": "Wash the tomatoes and green pepper; peel the cucumber and cut all the vegetables into medium-sized pieces.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-005.step.1": "Remove the garlic germ if you prefer a milder flavour.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-005.step.2": "Blend the tomatoes with the cucumber, pepper, onion and garlic first.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-005.step.3": "Slowly add the olive oil and wine vinegar while continuing to blend to emulsify the mixture.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-005.step.4": "Adjust the consistency with cold water, season with salt and strain if you want a smoother soup.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-005.step.5": "Chill in the refrigerator for at least 1 hour and serve very cold.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-005.ingredient.0": "ripe tomato",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-005.ingredient.1": "cucumber",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-005.ingredient.2": "green bell pepper",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-005.ingredient.3": "onion",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-005.ingredient.4": "garlic (clove)",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-005.ingredient.5": "olive oil",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-005.ingredient.6": "wine vinegar",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-005.ingredient.7": "cold water",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-005.ingredient.8": "salt",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-005.editorial.0": "Wash all vegetables eaten raw carefully and keep gazpacho refrigerated until serving. Wine vinegar may contain sulphites: check the label of the selected brand.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-005.editorial.1": "COMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: verify composition, allergens and traces for the exact items selected once official shop prices and product references are available. Do not claim \"allergen-free\" or \"trace-free\" before product verification.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-005.editorial.2": "Refrigeration: ≥ 60 min. This is not a total duration.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-006.title": "Traditional Spanish torrijas (milk-soaked French toast)",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-006.allergen": "Allergens identified from the listed ingredients: gluten (wheat), egg, milk.\n\nTorrijas contain egg, milk and wheat. Fry until the egg-containing interior is fully cooked, with no raw egg left inside. Refrigerate leftovers after cooling.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: verify composition, allergens and traces for the exact items selected once official shop prices and product references are available. Do not claim \"allergen-free\" or \"trace-free\" before product verification.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-006.step.0": "Warm the milk with some of the sugar, the cinnamon stick and the lemon peel without letting it boil; let it infuse for 10 minutes.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-006.step.1": "Cut the bread into thick slices and arrange them in a dish.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-006.step.2": "Strain the warm milk and pour it gradually over the bread, allowing it to soak without falling apart.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-006.step.3": "Beat the eggs, drain each slice lightly and dip it in the beaten egg.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-006.step.4": "Fry in batches in hot oil, browning both sides, then transfer to absorbent kitchen paper.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-006.step.5": "Mix the remaining sugar with the ground cinnamon, sprinkle over the torrijas and serve warm.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-006.ingredient.0": "day-old bread",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-006.ingredient.1": "whole milk",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-006.ingredient.2": "eggs",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-006.ingredient.3": "sugar",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-006.ingredient.4": "cinnamon stick",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-006.ingredient.5": "lemon peel",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-006.ingredient.6": "oil for frying",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-006.ingredient.7": "ground cinnamon",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-006.editorial.0": "Torrijas contain egg, milk and wheat. Fry until the egg-containing interior is fully cooked, with no raw egg left inside. Refrigerate leftovers after cooling.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-006.editorial.1": "COMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: verify composition, allergens and traces for the exact items selected once official shop prices and product references are available. Do not claim \"allergen-free\" or \"trace-free\" before product verification.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-006.editorial.2": "Infusion: 10 min. This is not a total duration.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-007.title": "Provençal ratatouille",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-007.allergen": "No mandatory allergens were identified in the declared simple ingredients; this does not prove the absence of allergens or traces.\n\nWash all vegetables thoroughly before cutting. Cook until tender, and refrigerate leftovers promptly rather than leaving them at room temperature for extended periods.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: verify composition, allergens and traces for the exact items selected once official shop prices and product references are available. Do not claim \"allergen-free\" or \"trace-free\" before product verification.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-007.step.0": "Dice the aubergine, courgette, red pepper and tomato into similarly sized pieces.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-007.step.1": "Brown the aubergine in a casserole with some of the oil, then remove it. Repeat with the courgette so it does not break down.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-007.step.2": "Sweat the onion and pepper in the remaining oil for 10 minutes; add the garlic and thyme.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-007.step.3": "Add the tomato and cook until it releases its juices and starts to reduce.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-007.step.4": "Return the aubergine and courgette to the casserole; cook covered for 15 minutes and uncovered for another 5 minutes.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-007.step.5": "Adjust the salt, add fresh basil and leave to rest for 5 minutes.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-007.ingredient.0": "aubergine (eggplant)",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-007.ingredient.1": "courgette (zucchini)",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-007.ingredient.2": "ripe tomato",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-007.ingredient.3": "red bell pepper",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-007.ingredient.4": "onion",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-007.ingredient.5": "garlic (cloves)",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-007.ingredient.6": "olive oil",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-007.ingredient.7": "thyme",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E03-007.ingredient.8": "basil",
