    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-183.title": "Chickpea chole masala",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-183.allergen": "No EU Annex II allergen directly identified in the declared ingredients; this does NOT certify absence of allergens or traces.\n\nUse fully cooked chickpeas, never raw or undercooked dried chickpeas; refrigerate leftovers promptly.\n\nLABEL VERIFICATION PENDING: when specific products, brands, SKUs and official store prices are available, verify actual ingredient labels, allergens and possible traces. Do not claim allergen-free status before checking.\n\nCOOKING TEST: the user confirmed preparing and tasting all ten recipes 41–50 and rated their flavour positively. No internal-temperature readings or measured yields were supplied; follow the food-safety instructions.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-183.step.0": "Peel and chop the onion, garlic and ginger; measure out the spices in advance so they do not burn.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-183.step.1": "Heat the oil and sauté the onion over medium heat for 8 minutes until golden at the edges.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-183.step.2": "Add the garlic, ginger, ground cumin and ground coriander; cook for 1 minute, stirring.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-183.step.3": "Add the crushed tomato, turmeric, chilli and salt; cook for 10 minutes until the sauce thickens slightly.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-183.step.4": "Add the chickpeas and water; simmer gently for 12 minutes, mashing a spoonful of chickpeas to thicken the sauce.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-183.step.5": "Turn off the heat, stir in the garam masala and lemon juice, let rest for 3 minutes and serve.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-183.ingredient.0": "cooked, drained chickpeas",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-183.ingredient.1": "crushed tomato",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-183.ingredient.2": "onion",
