    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-205.title": "Spinach and feta spanakopita",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-205.allergen": "Allergens identified from declared ingredients: gluten (wheat), milk, egg.\n\nThe pastry contains wheat and the filling contains egg and milk. Bake until the egg filling is completely set; refrigerate leftovers.\n\nLABEL VERIFICATION PENDING: when specific products, brands, SKUs and official store prices are available, verify actual ingredient labels, allergens and possible traces. Do not claim allergen-free status before checking.\n\nCOOKING TEST: the user confirmed preparing and tasting all ten recipes 41–50 and rated their flavour positively. No internal-temperature readings or measured yields were supplied; follow the food-safety instructions.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-205.step.0": "Wash and dry the spinach; sauté it in a large pan for 3 minutes, drain and gently squeeze out the water.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-205.step.1": "Sauté the chopped onion in 15 ml of olive oil for 5 minutes, then mix it with the spinach.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-205.step.2": "Crumble the feta and add the dill, beaten eggs, pepper and a little salt; fold in the cooled spinach.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-205.step.3": "Preheat the oven to 185 °C. Oil a 24 cm baking dish and lay in half the filo sheets, brushing each layer with oil.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-205.step.4": "Spread the filling evenly and cover with the remaining filo, brushing the layers with oil; fold in the edges and score portions with a knife.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-205.step.5": "Bake for 35–40 minutes until golden and the filling is fully set. Rest for 10 minutes before serving.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-205.ingredient.0": "fresh spinach",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-205.ingredient.1": "feta cheese",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-205.ingredient.2": "wheat filo pastry",
