    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-214.title": "Greek white bean fasolada",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-214.allergen": "Allergens identified from declared ingredients: celery.\n\nContains celery. Use fully cooked white beans; dried beans need proper cooking beforehand, which is not part of this recipe.\n\nLABEL VERIFICATION PENDING: when specific products, brands, SKUs and official store prices are available, verify actual ingredient labels, allergens and possible traces. Do not claim allergen-free status before checking.\n\nCOOKING TEST: the user confirmed preparing and tasting all ten recipes 41–50 and rated their flavour positively. No internal-temperature readings or measured yields were supplied; follow the food-safety instructions.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-214.step.0": "Peel the carrot, onion and garlic. Chop the celery and slice the carrot into thin half-moons.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-214.step.1": "Heat 40 ml of olive oil and sauté the onion, carrot and celery for 8 minutes.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-214.step.2": "Add the garlic and sweet paprika, stir for 30 seconds and immediately add the grated tomato so the paprika does not burn.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-214.step.3": "Cook for 8 minutes to concentrate the tomato; add the water and oregano and simmer for 15 minutes.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-214.step.4": "Add the drained cooked beans and simmer for another 12–15 minutes; mash a few beans to thicken the broth.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-214.step.5": "Finish with the remaining olive oil and a few drops of lemon juice; adjust the salt, rest for 5 minutes and serve.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-214.ingredient.0": "cooked drained white beans",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E04-214.ingredient.1": "ripe tomatoes",
