    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-059.title": "Basque tuna and potato marmitako",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-059.allergen": "Allergens identified from ingredients: fish.\n\nKeep the bonito chilled until it goes into the stew. Cook fish thoroughly (reference 63 °C, or opaque flesh that flakes easily) and avoid cross-contamination. Season with the salt already measured.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL REVIEW PENDING: once brands, exact product references and official store prices are available, check each package for ingredients, declared allergens, possible traces and storage instructions. Do not claim the dish is allergen-free before that review.\n\nCOOKING TEST FOR RECIPES 51–60: completed, with satisfactory taste, as confirmed by the user on 9 November 2026. No internal temperature readings or measured yields were provided.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-059.step.0": "Cut the bonito tuna into large cubes of about 3 cm and refrigerate while preparing the stew.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-059.step.1": "Chop the onion, peppers and garlic. Sauté in the olive oil for 10 minutes until softened.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-059.step.2": "Add the sweet paprika and crushed tomato; cook for 5 minutes, stirring.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-059.step.3": "Peel the potatoes and break them into irregular chunks with a knife to release starch; add them to the sautéed vegetables.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-059.step.4": "Cover with hot fish stock and cook for 18–22 minutes until the potatoes are tender.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-059.step.5": "Add the tuna and keep at a gentle simmer for 3–5 minutes, or until completely cooked through; serve with parsley. Season with the already measured salt before serving.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-059.ingredient.0": "fresh bonito tuna, boneless",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-059.ingredient.1": "potatoes",
