    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-101.title": "Coq au vin with chicken, mushrooms and red wine",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-101.allergen": "Allergens identified from ingredients: gluten (wheat).\n\nUse a thermometer to check that the thickest part of the chicken reaches 74 °C, without touching the bone. Wine may contain sulphites, and cooking does not guarantee complete removal of alcohol.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL REVIEW PENDING: once brands, exact product references and official store prices are available, check each package for ingredients, declared allergens, possible traces and storage instructions. Do not claim the dish is allergen-free before that review.\n\nCOOKING TEST FOR RECIPES 51–60: completed, with satisfactory taste, as confirmed by the user on 9 November 2026. No internal temperature readings or measured yields were provided.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-101.step.0": "Pat the chicken dry and brown it in a large casserole with olive oil for 4 minutes on each side. Remove it.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-101.step.1": "Brown the chopped cured pork belly, remove it, then add the pearl onions and carrot and cook for 6 minutes.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-101.step.2": "Add the garlic and flour, stir for 1 minute, then gradually pour in the wine, scraping the browned bits from the bottom.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-101.step.3": "Return the chicken and pork belly to the pot; add the chicken stock, thyme and bay leaf.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-101.step.4": "Cover and simmer on low heat for 75–90 minutes, until the chicken is tender and fully cooked through.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-101.step.5": "Brown the mushrooms separately and add them for the last 10 minutes. If the sauce is too thin, reduce it uncovered and adjust the salt.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-101.ingredient.0": "bone-in chicken thighs",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-101.ingredient.1": "cured pork belly",
