    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-114.title": "Niçoise salad with tuna and green beans",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-114.allergen": "Allergens identified from ingredients: fish, egg.\n\nCook the eggs and green beans thoroughly; if the beans are not tender after 5–7 minutes, continue cooking. Store tuna and anchovies as instructed on their labels. Check the vinegar for possible sulphites.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL REVIEW PENDING: once brands, exact product references and official store prices are available, check each package for ingredients, declared allergens, possible traces and storage instructions. Do not claim the dish is allergen-free before that review.\n\nCOOKING TEST FOR RECIPES 51–60: completed, with satisfactory taste, as confirmed by the user on 9 November 2026. No internal temperature readings or measured yields were provided.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-114.step.0": "Boil the eggs for 9–10 minutes, cool under running water and peel.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-114.step.1": "Trim the green beans and boil for 5–7 minutes until tender but still firm; cool and drain.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-114.step.2": "Wash and dry the lettuce leaves. Cut the tomatoes and red onion.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-114.step.3": "Whisk together the olive oil, wine vinegar and a pinch of salt for the dressing.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-114.step.4": "Divide the lettuce, tomatoes, green beans, tuna and black olives between four plates.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-114.step.5": "Add quartered eggs and anchovies, then drizzle with dressing immediately before eating.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-114.ingredient.0": "tomatoes",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-114.ingredient.1": "green beans",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-114.ingredient.2": "drained canned tuna",
