    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-126.title": "Homemade fermented Margherita pizza",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-126.allergen": "Allergens identified from ingredients: gluten (wheat), milk.\n\nThe 90–120-minute rise and 15-minute rest are additional waiting periods beyond the originally listed 40 minutes. Keep mozzarella refrigerated and bake until the base is fully cooked.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL REVIEW PENDING: once brands, exact product references and official store prices are available, check each package for ingredients, declared allergens, possible traces and storage instructions. Do not claim the dish is allergen-free before that review.\n\nCOOKING TEST FOR RECIPES 51–60: completed, with satisfactory taste, as confirmed by the user on 9 November 2026. No internal temperature readings or measured yields were provided.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-126.step.0": "Dissolve the yeast in the water, mix with the flour and salt, and knead for 10 minutes; work in 15 ml of olive oil.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-126.step.1": "Cover and leave the dough to rise for 90–120 minutes until roughly doubled in volume.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-126.step.2": "Divide into 4 balls and let relax for 15 minutes while preheating the oven with a baking tray to 250 °C.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-126.step.3": "Drain the mozzarella and season the crushed tomato lightly with the remaining 10 ml of olive oil.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-126.step.4": "Stretch each ball into a thin disc without flattening the rim too much, add the tomato sauce and distribute the mozzarella.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-126.step.5": "Bake each pizza for 9–13 minutes, depending on the oven, until the rim and base are golden. Finish with fresh basil.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-126.ingredient.0": "strong bread wheat flour",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-126.ingredient.1": "water",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-126.ingredient.2": "dried baker's yeast",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-126.ingredient.3": "salt",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-126.ingredient.4": "olive oil",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-126.ingredient.5": "crushed tomato",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-126.ingredient.6": "mozzarella",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-126.ingredient.7": "fresh basil",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-126.editorial.0": "Phase stated in the steps: 90–120 min. This is not a total duration.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-126.editorial.1": "Phase stated in the steps: 15 min. This is not a total duration.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-139.title": "Baked aubergine parmigiana",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-139.allergen": "Allergens identified from ingredients: milk.\n\nKeep the cheeses refrigerated. Allow the aubergine’s 10-minute rest and the final 10-minute settling time. Check whether the hard cheese contains egg-derived lysozyme.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL REVIEW PENDING: once brands, exact product references and official store prices are available, check each package for ingredients, declared allergens, possible traces and storage instructions. Do not claim the dish is allergen-free before that review.\n\nCOOKING TEST FOR RECIPES 51–60: completed, with satisfactory taste, as confirmed by the user on 9 November 2026. No internal temperature readings or measured yields were provided.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-139.step.0": "Slice the aubergines 1 cm thick; salt very lightly, rest for 10 minutes and pat dry.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-139.step.1": "Brush with 30 ml of olive oil and roast at 210 °C for 20 minutes, turning halfway through.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-139.step.2": "Sauté the chopped onion and garlic in the remaining oil for 7 minutes; add the crushed tomato and cook for 15 minutes.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-139.step.3": "In a baking dish, layer a little tomato sauce, aubergine, drained mozzarella, basil and hard cheese; repeat the layers.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-139.step.4": "Finish with sauce and a thin layer of cheese. Bake at 190 °C for 25–30 minutes until bubbling.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-139.step.5": "Rest for 10 minutes before cutting so the layers hold together.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-139.ingredient.0": "aubergines",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-139.ingredient.1": "crushed tomato",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-139.ingredient.2": "mozzarella",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-139.ingredient.3": "hard Parmesan-style cheese",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-139.ingredient.4": "onion",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-139.ingredient.5": "garlic",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-139.ingredient.6": "olive oil",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-139.ingredient.7": "basil",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-139.ingredient.8": "salt",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-139.editorial.0": "Phase stated in the steps: 10 min. This is not a total duration.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-139.editorial.1": "Phase stated in the steps: 10 min. This is not a total duration.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-153.title": "Indonesian beef rendang with coconut",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-153.allergen": "No mandatory-declaration allergen group identified directly from the ingredients; this does not mean free from traces.\n\nCook the beef thoroughly until tender. Stir while reducing so the coconut does not burn; remove fibrous lemongrass stalks and lime leaves before serving. Do not assume the packaged products are allergen-free without their labels.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL REVIEW PENDING: once brands, exact product references and official store prices are available, check each package for ingredients, declared allergens, possible traces and storage instructions. Do not claim the dish is allergen-free before that review.\n\nCOOKING TEST FOR RECIPES 51–60: completed, with satisfactory taste, as confirmed by the user on 9 November 2026. No internal temperature readings or measured yields were provided.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-153.step.0": "Blend the shallots, garlic, ginger, galangal, chilli and turmeric with a little coconut milk into a paste.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-153.step.1": "Heat the oil in a heavy pot and fry the paste for 5 minutes until fragrant.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-153.step.2": "Add the beef cut into 4 cm cubes, remaining coconut milk, bruised lemongrass and kaffir lime leaves.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-153.step.3": "Simmer uncovered over low heat for about 2 hours, stirring to prevent sticking to the bottom.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-153.step.4": "Toast the unsweetened grated coconut in a dry pan for 3 minutes and add it to the pot.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-153.step.5": "Keep reducing for 30–50 minutes until the sauce is thick, dark and clings to the meat; check that the beef is tender and season with salt.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-153.ingredient.0": "beef for stewing",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-153.ingredient.1": "coconut milk",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-153.ingredient.2": "shallots",
