    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-156.title": "Indonesian chicken soto ayam with noodles",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-156.allergen": "Allergens identified from ingredients: egg.\n\nCook chicken completely to 74 °C and cook sprouts thoroughly before serving, especially for vulnerable people; a brief blanch may be insufficient. Sprouts may come from soybean or mung bean: verify the species and label before assigning the soy allergen. Season with the measured salt.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL REVIEW PENDING: once brands, exact product references and official store prices are available, check each package for ingredients, declared allergens, possible traces and storage instructions. Do not claim the dish is allergen-free before that review.\n\nCOOKING TEST FOR RECIPES 51–60: completed, with satisfactory taste, as confirmed by the user on 9 November 2026. No internal temperature readings or measured yields were provided.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-156.step.0": "Boil the eggs for 10 minutes, cool, peel and set aside cut into halves.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-156.step.1": "Blend the shallots, garlic, ginger, fresh turmeric and galangal; fry this paste in the oil for 5 minutes.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-156.step.2": "Add the chicken, bruised lemongrass and stock. Simmer gently for 35–40 minutes until the chicken is fully cooked.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-156.step.3": "Remove the chicken, shred it and return the meat to the broth without bones or skin.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-156.step.4": "Prepare the rice noodles according to the packet instructions and briefly blanch the bean sprouts.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-156.step.5": "Serve in bowls with noodles, chicken and broth, bean sprouts, egg and lime wedges. Season with the already measured salt before serving.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-156.ingredient.0": "chicken thigh meat",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-156.ingredient.1": "water or homemade stock",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-156.ingredient.2": "rice noodles",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-156.ingredient.3": "shallots",
