    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-177.editorial.0": "Phase stated in the steps: 30 min. This is not a total duration.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-189.title": "Smoky aubergine baingan bharta",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-189.allergen": "No mandatory allergens are directly identified in the listed ingredients. Roast the aubergine thoroughly, wash tomatoes and coriander, and check spice labels. Suggested rice is not included in the shopping list.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: once specific items, brands and official store prices are available, inspect full ingredients, declared allergens, possible traces and storage instructions on the package. Price does not certify allergen status.\n\nCOOKING TEST 61–70: the user confirms cooking and tasting this recipe and reports a satisfactory flavour. This confirmation does not include measured core temperatures, yield measurements, or food-safety testing.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-189.step.0": "Prick the aubergines and roast them whole at 220 °C for 30–35 minutes, until their flesh is very soft.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-189.step.1": "Let cool slightly, remove the charred skin and mash the flesh with a fork.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-189.step.2": "Sauté the chopped onion in oil for 7 minutes; add the garlic, ginger and green chilli.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-189.step.3": "Stir in the cumin and turmeric for 30 seconds, then add the chopped tomatoes and cook for 10 minutes.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-189.step.4": "Add the mashed aubergine and cook for another 5 minutes to blend the flavours.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-189.step.5": "Season and finish with fresh coriander. Serve with rice if you wish to keep the dish gluten-free.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-189.ingredient.0": "aubergines",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-189.ingredient.1": "tomatoes",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-189.ingredient.2": "onion",
