    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-189.editorial.0": "Phase stated in the steps: 30–35 min. This is not a total duration.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-203.title": "Pork souvlaki with lemon and oregano",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-203.allergen": "CONTAINS GLUTEN: wheat pita. Marinate pork chilled (≤4 °C); for whole-cut pork pieces verify at least 63 °C followed by a 3-minute rest using a thermometer. Handle warmed pita safely.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: once specific items, brands and official store prices are available, inspect full ingredients, declared allergens, possible traces and storage instructions on the package. Price does not certify allergen status.\n\nCOOKING TEST 61–70: the user confirms cooking and tasting this recipe and reports a satisfactory flavour. This confirmation does not include measured core temperatures, yield measurements, or food-safety testing.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-203.step.0": "Cut the pork into 3 cm cubes and toss with the oil, juice of one lemon, garlic, oregano, salt and pepper.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-203.step.1": "Marinate covered in the refrigerator for 30–60 minutes; if using wooden skewers, soak them in water.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-203.step.2": "Cut the red onion and green pepper into similarly sized pieces.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-203.step.3": "Thread pork and vegetables onto skewers, leaving small gaps so heat can circulate.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-203.step.4": "Grill over high heat for 12–15 minutes, turning regularly, until the pork is thoroughly cooked.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-203.step.5": "Serve with warmed pita, wedges from the second lemon and the grilled vegetables.",
