    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-207.title": "Dolmades stuffed with rice and herbs",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-207.allergen": "No mandatory allergens directly identified. Check preservatives and possible sulphites in packaged vine leaves. Cook rice fully; cool and refrigerate leftovers promptly rather than leaving them at room temperature.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: once specific items, brands and official store prices are available, inspect full ingredients, declared allergens, possible traces and storage instructions on the package. Price does not certify allergen status.\n\nCOOKING TEST 61–70: the user confirms cooking and tasting this recipe and reports a satisfactory flavour. This confirmation does not include measured core temperatures, yield measurements, or food-safety testing.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-207.step.0": "Rinse the preserved vine leaves under cold water to remove excess salt; drain them.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-207.step.1": "Sauté the finely chopped onion in 25 ml of olive oil for 7 minutes; add the rice and stir for one minute.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-207.step.2": "Remove from the heat and mix with dill, parsley, zest of one lemon, salt and black pepper.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-207.step.3": "Put a spoonful of filling on each leaf, fold in the sides and roll loosely because the rice expands.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-207.step.4": "Line a pot with torn leaves, pack the rolls closely together, add water, lemon juice and the remaining oil. Cover with a small heatproof plate.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-207.step.5": "Cook over very low heat for 35–45 minutes until the rice is tender; allow to cool slightly before serving.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-207.ingredient.0": "preserved vine leaves",
