    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-227.title": "Mexican carnitas tacos",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-227.allergen": "No mandatory allergens directly identified if tortillas are 100% corn; check labels for wheat and traces. Fully cook the pork; reserve garnishing onion before it contacts raw meat.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: once specific items, brands and official store prices are available, inspect full ingredients, declared allergens, possible traces and storage instructions on the package. Price does not certify allergen status.\n\nCOOKING TEST 61–70: the user confirms cooking and tasting this recipe and reports a satisfactory flavour. This confirmation does not include measured core temperatures, yield measurements, or food-safety testing.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-227.step.0": "Cut the pork into large cubes. Reserve some of the onion for serving, then put the rest in a pot with the pork, garlic, orange juice, water, bay leaves, oregano, cumin and salt.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-227.step.1": "Cover and simmer on very low heat for 90–110 minutes, until the meat shreds easily.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-227.step.2": "Uncover and allow the liquid to reduce, stirring so it does not stick.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-227.step.3": "Partly shred the meat and brown it for 5 minutes in a hot pan in its own fat.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-227.step.4": "Warm the corn tortillas in a dry pan for about 20 seconds per side.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-227.step.5": "Fill the tortillas with meat and finish with coriander, some reserved chopped onion and lime.",
