    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-231.title": "Mexican red pozole with hominy and pork",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-231.allergen": "No mandatory allergens directly identified; check precooked hominy and packaged chilli labels. Cook pork thoroughly, use 2,000 ml of water for simmering and the remaining 400 ml for soaking chillies; wash raw garnishes.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: once specific items, brands and official store prices are available, inspect full ingredients, declared allergens, possible traces and storage instructions on the package. Price does not certify allergen status.\n\nCOOKING TEST 61–70: the user confirms cooking and tasting this recipe and reports a satisfactory flavour. This confirmation does not include measured core temperatures, yield measurements, or food-safety testing.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-231.step.0": "Simmer the pork pieces with half the onion and 2 litres of water for about 75 minutes; skim impurities from the broth.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-231.step.1": "Open the dried chillies, remove the seeds and toast for 10–15 seconds per side without burning them.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-231.step.2": "Soak the chillies in the remaining 400 ml of hot water for 15 minutes, blend with the garlic and a ladle of broth, then strain.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-231.step.3": "Pour the chilli sauce into the pot and cook for 10 minutes; add the drained, precooked hominy.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-231.step.4": "Cook for another 20 minutes until the pork and hominy are tender; adjust the salt.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-231.step.5": "Serve topped with finely shredded lettuce, radishes, oregano, chopped onion and lime.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-231.ingredient.0": "drained precooked pozole hominy",
