    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-254.title": "Steamed baozi with pork and cabbage filling",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-254.allergen": "CONTAINS GLUTEN (wheat), SOY and SESAME. Check soy sauce for wheat as well as the wheat flour. Ground pork filling must reach 71 °C at the centre; steaming time alone does not prove safety.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: once specific items, brands and official store prices are available, inspect full ingredients, declared allergens, possible traces and storage instructions on the package. Price does not certify allergen status.\n\nCOOKING TEST 61–70: the user confirms cooking and tasting this recipe and reports a satisfactory flavour. This confirmation does not include measured core temperatures, yield measurements, or food-safety testing.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-254.step.0": "Mix the flour, warm water, dried yeast, sugar and 2 g of salt; knead for 8 minutes to make an elastic dough.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-254.step.1": "Leave covered to rise for 60–75 minutes, until almost doubled in volume.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-254.step.2": "Finely chop the cabbage, sprinkle with 2 g of salt, wait 10 minutes and squeeze out the water.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-254.step.3": "Mix the cabbage with minced pork, spring onion, ginger, soy sauce and sesame oil; divide the filling into eight portions.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-254.step.4": "Divide the dough into eight pieces, flatten each into a round with a thicker centre and pinch the edges closed over the filling.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-254.step.5": "Rest for 15 minutes on individual paper squares, then steam in batches for 16–20 minutes; check that the pork filling is thoroughly cooked before serving.",
