    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-258.title": "Homemade glazed char siu pork",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-258.allergen": "CONTAINS SOY; hoisin and soy sauce may also contain WHEAT/GLUTEN or SESAME depending on brand. Reserve clean glaze before raw pork contact, refrigerate while marinating, and verify at least 63 °C internally plus 3 minutes resting for pork loin.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: once specific items, brands and official store prices are available, inspect full ingredients, declared allergens, possible traces and storage instructions on the package. Price does not certify allergen status.\n\nCOOKING TEST 61–70: the user confirms cooking and tasting this recipe and reports a satisfactory flavour. This confirmation does not include measured core temperatures, yield measurements, or food-safety testing.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-258.step.0": "Mix soy sauce, hoisin sauce, honey, rice vinegar, grated garlic, ginger and Chinese five-spice powder.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-258.step.1": "Set aside 3 tablespoons of the marinade before it comes into contact with the raw pork.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-258.step.2": "Coat the pork with the rest and marinate covered in the refrigerator for 2–6 hours.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-258.step.3": "Place the pork on a rack over a roasting tray with water underneath; roast at 190 °C for 30–40 minutes until thoroughly cooked.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-258.step.4": "Boil the reserved, uncontaminated marinade separately with a little water to make a glaze, and brush it on during the final 8 minutes.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-258.step.5": "Rest the meat for 8 minutes before slicing; serve over rice or vegetables, which are not included in the ingredients.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-258.ingredient.0": "pork loin",
