    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-289.title": "Thai chicken and herb larb gai",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-289.allergen": "CONTAINS FISH: fish sauce; crustaceans are possible depending on label. Ground chicken must reach 74 °C at the centre before being mixed with cleaned herbs and vegetables; avoid cross-contamination.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: once specific items, brands and official store prices are available, inspect full ingredients, declared allergens, possible traces and storage instructions on the package. Price does not certify allergen status.\n\nCOOKING TEST 61–70: the user confirms cooking and tasting this recipe and reports a satisfactory flavour. This confirmation does not include measured core temperatures, yield measurements, or food-safety testing.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-289.step.0": "Toast the uncooked rice in a dry pan over medium heat until golden, 6–8 minutes. Let cool, then grind to fine granules.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-289.step.1": "Cook the minced chicken in a pan with the water, stirring to break it into small pieces; let the liquid evaporate and ensure the chicken is thoroughly cooked.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-289.step.2": "Take the pan off the heat and mix the chicken with fish sauce, lime juice, sugar and chopped red chilli.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-289.step.3": "Add the finely sliced shallots and spring onion.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-289.step.4": "Fold in the mint, coriander and ground toasted rice, stirring gently.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E05-289.step.5": "Serve warm over clean lettuce leaves; adjust the heat and acidity to taste.",
