    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-102.title": "Beef bourguignon with mushrooms",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-102.allergen": "CONTAINS GLUTEN: wheat flour. Check wine sulphites and beef stock and pancetta labels; cooking does not guarantee removal of all alcohol. Keep beef chilled before cooking.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL PENDING: when store-specific SKUs, brands, label photos or product sheets and official prices are available, verify composition, declared allergens, possible traces, pack sizes and storage. Price alone is not allergen evidence. Do not claim “trace-free”.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-102.step.0": "Pat the beef dry and brown it in the listed olive oil in batches without overcrowding the pot.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-102.step.1": "Brown the bacon and add the pearl onions and carrots; cook for seven minutes.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-102.step.2": "Stir in the garlic, tomato paste and flour, cooking for one minute.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-102.step.3": "Pour in the red wine and deglaze the pot; add the beef stock, thyme and bay leaves.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-102.step.4": "Return the beef and cook covered over very low heat for 2–2.5 hours, until tender.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-102.step.5": "Sauté the mushrooms separately and add them for the final fifteen minutes.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-102.step.6": "Reduce the sauce uncovered if needed, season with the listed salt and remove the bay leaves before serving.",
