    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-135.title": "Saffron risotto alla milanese",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-135.allergen": "CONTAINS MILK: butter and Parmesan. Check vegetable stock for celery. Serve freshly made; cool leftover rice quickly and refrigerate it.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL PENDING: when store-specific SKUs, brands, label photos or product sheets and official prices are available, verify composition, declared allergens, possible traces, pack sizes and storage. Price alone is not allergen evidence. Do not claim “trace-free”.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-135.step.0": "Keep the vegetable stock hot and steep the saffron in a cup of stock.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-135.step.1": "Gently cook the onion in olive oil and a little butter without browning it.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-135.step.2": "Add the rice and stir for two minutes to lightly toast the grains.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-135.step.3": "Add the stock one ladle at a time, waiting until the previous ladle has been absorbed.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-135.step.4": "Halfway through cooking, add the saffron and continue cooking for 16–19 minutes until the rice is al dente.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-135.step.5": "Turn off the heat and emulsify with the remaining butter and Parmesan.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-135.step.6": "Season with the listed salt and pepper and serve immediately; the risotto should flow softly, never be stiff.",
