    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-179.title": "Chicken biryani with basmati rice",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-179.allergen": "CONTAINS MILK: yoghurt. Marinate chicken in the fridge (≤4 °C) and verify 74 °C at its centre with a thermometer. Cool leftover rice promptly and refrigerate.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL PENDING: when store-specific SKUs, brands, label photos or product sheets and official prices are available, verify composition, declared allergens, possible traces, pack sizes and storage. Price alone is not allergen evidence. Do not claim “trace-free”.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-179.step.0": "Marinate the chicken with yogurt, garlic, ginger, spices and the listed salt for thirty minutes in the refrigerator.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-179.step.1": "Wash and soak the basmati rice for twenty minutes; steep the saffron in the listed 30 ml of milk or water.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-179.step.2": "Brown the onion in oil, reserve half and sauté the chicken with the rest for fifteen minutes.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-179.step.3": "Parboil the rice in plenty of water with cardamom and cinnamon for five or six minutes, until half-cooked.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-179.step.4": "Layer the rice over the chicken and add mint, coriander, reserved onion and saffron.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-179.step.5": "Seal the pot tightly and finish over very low heat for 20–25 minutes.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-179.step.6": "Ensure the chicken is fully cooked, rest for ten minutes and serve in layers.",
