    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-229.title": "Baja-style crispy fish tacos",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-229.allergen": "CONTAINS FISH, GLUTEN (wheat) AND MILK (yoghurt). Cook fish to 63 °C internally or until opaque and flaky; 175 °C is the OIL temperature, not the fish temperature. Refrigerate the sauce.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL PENDING: when store-specific SKUs, brands, label photos or product sheets and official prices are available, verify composition, declared allergens, possible traces, pack sizes and storage. Price alone is not allergen evidence. Do not claim “trace-free”.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-229.step.0": "Cut the boneless white fish into twelve strips and check carefully for any bones.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-229.step.1": "Mix the shredded cabbage with the juice of one lime for the slaw.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-229.step.2": "Mix the yogurt with coriander and another lime for the sauce; refrigerate it.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-229.step.3": "Whisk the flour, cold sparkling water, paprika and salt to make the batter.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-229.step.4": "Coat the fish and fry in batches in oil at 175 °C until golden and fully cooked.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-229.step.5": "Drain on a rack and warm the corn tortillas in a pan.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E06-229.step.6": "Assemble the tacos with cabbage, fish, sauce, radishes and the remaining lime.",
