    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-057.title": "Galician-style octopus with potatoes",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-057.allergen": "CONTAINS MOLLUSCS (octopus). Use octopus from an approved supplier, thaw in the refrigerator and cook thoroughly. Avoid cross-contact with other food; cool and refrigerate leftovers promptly.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: once exact products, SKUs and official store prices are available, check brand, composition, allergens, possible traces, batch and storage. A price does not establish allergen safety.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-057.step.0": "If the octopus is fresh, clean and freeze it first according to the supplier's guidance; thaw in the refrigerator. For previously frozen octopus, follow the label.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-057.step.1": "Bring the water to the boil with the onion and bay leaf. Dip the octopus in three times for a few seconds each, then leave it in the pot.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-057.step.2": "Simmer gently for about 35–50 minutes depending on size. Test the thickest part of a tentacle with a skewer: it should be tender rather than relying on a fixed time.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-057.step.3": "Cook the washed potatoes in separate water for 20–25 minutes, or until a knife passes through them. Drain and let cool slightly.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-057.step.4": "Rest the octopus off the heat for 5 minutes. Cut the tentacles into 1–2 cm slices using clean scissors.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-057.step.5": "Cut the potatoes into thick slices, arrange the octopus on top, sprinkle with coarse salt, sweet paprika and a pinch of hot paprika, and finish with the uncooked olive oil.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-057.step.6": "Serve hot; refrigerate leftovers promptly and consume them in line with official storage recommendations.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-057.ingredient.0": "raw cleaned octopus",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-057.ingredient.1": "medium potatoes",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-057.ingredient.2": "onion",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-057.ingredient.3": "extra virgin olive oil",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-057.ingredient.4": "sweet paprika",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-057.ingredient.5": "hot paprika",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-057.ingredient.6": "coarse salt",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-057.ingredient.7": "cooking water",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-057.ingredient.8": "bay leaf (leaf)",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-057.editorial.0": "CONTAINS MOLLUSCS (octopus). Use octopus from an approved supplier, thaw in the refrigerator and cook thoroughly. Avoid cross-contact with other food; cool and refrigerate leftovers promptly.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-057.editorial.1": "COMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: verify brand, SKU, ingredients, allergens, traces, batch and storage once exact products and official store prices are available. Price does not validate a label.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-143.title": "Tuscan ribollita with beans and cabbage",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-143.allergen": "CONTAINS GLUTEN (wheat bread) and CELERY. Check the bread and packaged beans; reheat leftovers thoroughly. Never claim freedom from traces without the actual labels.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: once exact products, SKUs and official store prices are available, check brand, composition, allergens, possible traces, batch and storage. A price does not establish allergen safety.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-143.step.0": "Wash the vegetables. Chop the onion, celery and garlic; dice the carrots and slice the cabbages, removing any very tough ribs.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-143.step.1": "Heat 35 ml of the oil in a pot and gently fry the onion, celery, carrot and garlic for 8–10 minutes without burning.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-143.step.2": "Add the tomatoes and rosemary, stir for 2 minutes, then add the cabbages and sauté for 3 minutes until they begin to soften.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-143.step.3": "Blend approximately one third of the beans with 150 ml of the water to make a thick base.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-143.step.4": "Add the remaining water, whole beans and bean purée. Simmer for 30 minutes, stirring occasionally.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-143.step.5": "Tear the bread into medium pieces, add it and cook for another 12–15 minutes. It should be a thick stew, not a thin soup.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-143.step.6": "Turn off the heat, adjust the salt and add pepper. Rest for 10 minutes; serve with the remaining 20 ml of oil.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-143.step.7": "If saving for another day, refrigerate without delay and reheat thoroughly before serving; add a little water if it has become too thick.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-143.ingredient.0": "cooked drained white beans",
