    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-185.title": "Rajma masala: red kidney bean curry with basmati rice",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-185.allergen": "No Annex II allergen is directly identified in the declared simple ingredients; this does NOT mean “allergen-free”. Use properly cooked canned kidney beans, never inadequately boiled dried beans. Cool and refrigerate leftover rice promptly; check spice blends and labels.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: once exact products, SKUs and official store prices are available, check brand, composition, allergens, possible traces, batch and storage. A price does not establish allergen safety.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-185.step.0": "Rinse and drain the canned kidney beans. Do not use dried kidney beans that have not been boiled sufficiently.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-185.step.1": "Chop the onion, garlic and ginger. Grate or blend the tomatoes without adding water.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-185.step.2": "Fry the onion in the oil for about 8 minutes. Add the garlic and ginger for 1 minute.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-185.step.3": "Add cumin, ground coriander, turmeric and paprika; stir for 30 seconds, then add the tomato to prevent the spices burning.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-185.step.4": "Cook the tomatoes for 8–10 minutes until reduced. Add the beans, 250 ml water and salt. Simmer for 12–15 minutes.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-185.step.5": "Mash about one fifth of the beans with a spoon to thicken the sauce; stir in the garam masala at the end and check the salt.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-185.step.6": "While the curry cooks, rinse the basmati, combine with 450 ml water and cook covered following the packet, normally 12–15 minutes. Rest for 5 minutes.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-185.step.7": "Serve the rajma with rice and fresh coriander. Cool leftover cooked rice rapidly and refrigerate.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-185.ingredient.0": "canned kidney beans, drained",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-185.ingredient.1": "uncooked basmati rice",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-185.ingredient.2": "water for cooking rice",
