    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-212.title": "Greek gigantes plaki: baked giant beans",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-212.allergen": "CONTAINS CELERY. Use pre-cooked beans and check packaged bean and tomato labels. Refrigerate leftovers promptly and reheat thoroughly.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: once exact products, SKUs and official store prices are available, check brand, composition, allergens, possible traces, batch and storage. A price does not establish allergen safety.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-212.step.0": "Preheat the oven to 190 °C using top and bottom heat. Drain and rinse the cooked giant beans.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-212.step.1": "Finely dice the onion, carrots and celery; chop the garlic, dill and parsley separately.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-212.step.2": "Heat 30 ml of oil and fry the onion, celery and carrots for 8–10 minutes until softened.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-212.step.3": "Add the garlic for 30 seconds. Stir in tomatoes, water, oregano, pepper and salt; simmer for 8 minutes.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-212.step.4": "Mix the beans with the sauce and half the dill in a wide baking dish; drizzle the remaining 25 ml oil over the top.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-212.step.5": "Bake uncovered for 25–30 minutes, until the sauce is thick and lightly toasted around the edges without drying out the beans.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-212.step.6": "Remove from the oven, rest for 5 minutes and finish with the remaining dill and fresh parsley.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-212.step.7": "Serve hot or warm; keep leftovers covered in the refrigerator.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-212.ingredient.0": "cooked drained giant beans",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E07-212.ingredient.1": "crushed tomatoes",
