    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-011.title": "Canarian carne de fiesta with potatoes",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-011.allergen": "White wine and vinegar: check labels for SULPHITES and the relevant final concentration. Marinate pork for 4–12 hours in the refrigerator; thoroughly cook the meat and any reused marinade. Cooking does not guarantee all wine alcohol has evaporated.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: once exact products, SKUs and official store prices are available, check brand, composition, allergens, possible traces, batch and storage. A price does not establish allergen safety.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-011.step.0": "Cut the pork into roughly 3 cm cubes and keep refrigerated while preparing the marinade.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-011.step.1": "Crush the garlic with the cumin, oregano, thyme and salt. Mix in the paprika, wine, vinegar and 25 ml oil.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-011.step.2": "Combine the meat, marinade and bay leaves in a covered container. Refrigerate for 4–12 hours; do not marinate at room temperature.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-011.step.3": "Remove the meat from the marinade, reserving the liquid separately. Heat 25 ml oil in a large casserole and brown the meat in batches without overcrowding.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-011.step.4": "Return all the pork to the casserole, add the reserved marinade and 60 ml water. Cover and simmer over medium heat for 20–25 minutes, then uncover for the last 5 minutes until reduced and the meat is thoroughly cooked.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-011.step.5": "Meanwhile, cut the potatoes into wedges. Toss with 15 ml oil and roast at 210 °C for 30–35 minutes, turning halfway through, until golden.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-011.step.6": "Check that the pork is fully cooked, adjust the salt and serve with the potatoes and chopped parsley. Never reuse uncooked marinade unless thoroughly boiled/cooked.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-011.ingredient.0": "boneless lean pork or pork shoulder",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-011.ingredient.1": "potatoes for frying or roasting",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-011.ingredient.2": "peeled garlic",
