    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-011.editorial.1": "COMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: verify brand, SKU, ingredients, allergens, traces, batch and storage once exact products and official store prices are available. Price does not validate a label.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-117.title": "French moules marinières (mussels in white wine)",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-117.allergen": "CONTAINS MOLLUSCS (mussels) and MILK (butter). Check wine for possible SULPHITES. Buy mussels from an approved source, keep chilled, discard broken shells and those that do not close before cooking, and any that stay closed afterward. Serve immediately.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: once exact products, SKUs and official store prices are available, check brand, composition, allergens, possible traces, batch and storage. A price does not establish allergen safety.\n\nNOTICE: cooking wine can leave residual alcohol; cooking does not guarantee complete removal.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-117.step.0": "Keep mussels refrigerated until use. Discard broken shells and open mussels that do not close when tapped. Rinse under cold water and remove beards just before cooking.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-117.step.1": "Finely chop shallots and garlic; wash and dry the parsley and cut the lemon into wedges.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-117.step.2": "In a wide covered pot, melt the butter over medium heat and cook the shallots for 3 minutes without browning. Add garlic and thyme for 30 seconds.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-117.step.3": "Pour in the white wine and water, add the bay leaf and boil for 2 minutes.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-117.step.4": "Add the cleaned mussels and cover. Cook over high heat for 5–7 minutes, shaking the pot a couple of times to distribute heat.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-117.step.5": "Remove from heat when the mussels are open and thoroughly cooked. Discard any that remain closed; do not force them open.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-117.step.6": "Add pepper and parsley. Serve immediately with the cooking liquor strained to remove sediment and lemon wedges. Do not leave cooked mussels unrefrigerated for prolonged periods.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-117.ingredient.0": "fresh mussels in shells",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-117.ingredient.1": "shallots",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-117.ingredient.2": "butter",
