    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-244.editorial.1": "COMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: verify brand, SKU, ingredients, allergens, traces, batch and storage once exact products and official store prices are available. Price does not validate a label.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-271.title": "Sichuan yu xiang aubergine with rice",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-271.allergen": "CONTAINS SOY (soy sauce) and SESAME (oil). Doubanjiang and soy sauce may contain WHEAT/GLUTEN; check labels for these and possible animal-derived ingredients. Cool and refrigerate leftover rice promptly.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: once exact products, SKUs and official store prices are available, check brand, composition, allergens, possible traces, batch and storage. A price does not establish allergen safety.\n\nEDITORIAL NOTE: optional pre-salting of the aubergine mentions salt without a specified amount or a measured ingredient. Do not automatically add it to the shopping list; this optional technique may be skipped.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-271.step.0": "Rinse the rice until the water is less cloudy. Cook it with 450 ml water according to the packet; rest covered for 5 minutes.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-271.step.1": "Cut the aubergine into evenly sized batons. If very large or bitter, salt lightly for 10 minutes, rinse and dry thoroughly; otherwise just pat dry.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-271.step.2": "Dissolve the cornflour in 170 ml cold water and mix in the soy sauce, vinegar and sugar to make a smooth sauce.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-271.step.3": "Heat half the vegetable oil in a wide pan over medium-high heat. Brown the aubergine in two batches for 8–10 minutes total until tender; add small amounts of water and cover briefly if needed.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-271.step.4": "Lower the heat. Add the remaining oil and fry garlic, ginger, the white parts of spring onions and optional chilli for 30 seconds. Add doubanjiang and stir for 30 seconds more.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-271.step.5": "Return the aubergine to the pan, pour in the sauce and cook for 2–4 minutes, stirring gently, until thickened and coating the aubergine.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-271.step.6": "Turn off the heat, add the sesame oil and green parts of the spring onions, and serve with the rice. Check the doubanjiang label: some brands contain wheat, soy and other animal-derived ingredients.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-271.ingredient.0": "aubergine",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-271.ingredient.1": "dry jasmine rice",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-271.ingredient.2": "water for rice",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-271.ingredient.3": "garlic",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-271.ingredient.4": "fresh ginger",
