    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-271.ingredient.14": "optional hot red pepper",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-271.editorial.0": "CONTAINS SOY (soy sauce) and SESAME (oil). Doubanjiang and soy sauce may contain WHEAT/GLUTEN; check labels for these and possible animal-derived ingredients. Cool and refrigerate leftover rice promptly.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-271.editorial.1": "COMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: verify brand, SKU, ingredients, allergens, traces, batch and storage once exact products and official store prices are available. Price does not validate a label.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-281.title": "Massaman beef curry with potatoes and peanuts",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-281.allergen": "CONTAINS PEANUTS and FISH (fish sauce). Commercial massaman paste may contain CRUSTACEANS (shrimp paste), soy or gluten: check the brand. Cook beef thoroughly and cool/refrigerate leftover rice promptly.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: once exact products, SKUs and official store prices are available, check brand, composition, allergens, possible traces, batch and storage. A price does not establish allergen safety.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-281.step.0": "Cut the beef into even cubes about 3 cm across and pat dry with kitchen paper. Peel and dice the potatoes into 3 cm cubes; cut the onion into thick wedges.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-281.step.1": "Heat the oil in a casserole and sear the beef in two batches, 2–3 minutes per side, until browned outside. Set aside.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-281.step.2": "Add 100 ml of the thick part of the coconut milk and the massaman paste to the casserole. Cook over medium heat for 2 minutes, stirring until fragrant without burning.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-281.step.3": "Return the beef, then add the remaining coconut milk, 300 ml water, cinnamon, star anise and onion. Bring to a gentle simmer, cover and cook 80–95 minutes until the meat starts to soften.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-281.step.4": "Add the potatoes, tamarind, sugar, fish sauce and 45 g peanuts. Continue for 25–30 minutes until the potatoes are tender and the beef thoroughly cooked and meltingly soft; add water if it becomes too dry.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-281.step.5": "Meanwhile rinse and cook the jasmine rice with 420 ml water, following the packet. Let rest covered for five minutes.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-281.step.6": "Taste the sauce and balance salty, sour and sweet without automatically adding more salt. Remove the cinnamon and star anise before serving. Top with 25 g peanuts, the optional 5 g fresh coriander and lime wedges; serve the rice separately.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-281.ingredient.0": "diced stewing beef",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-281.ingredient.1": "waxy potatoes",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-281.ingredient.2": "onion",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-281.ingredient.3": "unsweetened coconut milk",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-281.ingredient.4": "massaman curry paste",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-281.ingredient.5": "unsalted roasted peanuts",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-281.ingredient.6": "tamarind paste",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-281.ingredient.7": "fish sauce",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-281.ingredient.8": "brown sugar",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-281.ingredient.9": "cinnamon stick",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-281.ingredient.10": "star anise",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-281.ingredient.11": "vegetable oil",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E08-281.ingredient.12": "water",
