    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-003.title": "Shiitake, ginger and spring-onion congee",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-003.allergen": "CONTAINS WHEAT/GLUTEN, SOY AND SESAME from regular soy sauce and sesame oil/seeds. Cool leftover cooked rice promptly and refrigerate; never keep congee lukewarm for hours. The extra 100–200 ml water is conditional, not a fixed basket quantity.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: once brand, SKU, products and official prices by store and format are available, verify ingredients, allergens and possible cross-contact against the actual label. Price alone does not certify food safety.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-003.step.0": "Wash the spring onions and mushrooms. Clean the shiitake with damp kitchen paper, remove very tough stems and slice the caps. Peel the ginger and cut into thin strips.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-003.step.1": "Rinse the rice twice in cold water without soaking it; drain in a fine sieve to remove excess surface starch.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-003.step.2": "Pour 1.6 litres of water into a tall pan, add the rice and half the ginger, and bring to a gentle boil. Reduce to low heat.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-003.step.3": "Cook with the lid ajar for 45–55 minutes, stirring the bottom every 8–10 minutes to prevent sticking. Add another 100–200 ml of hot water only if it thickens too much.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-003.step.4": "Once the grains have broken down and the texture is creamy, season very sparingly with the measured salt, as the soy sauce is already salty. Turn off the heat and rest for five minutes.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-003.step.5": "While the rice cooks, heat 15 ml of vegetable oil and sauté the shiitake for 5–7 minutes until they lose moisture and colour lightly. Add the chopped garlic and remaining ginger for one minute.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-003.step.6": "Add the labelled soy sauce to the mushrooms and stir for half a minute. Slice the spring onions into rings, reserving their green tops for finishing.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-003.step.7": "Serve hot in four bowls with the mushrooms, a drizzle of sesame oil, spring onions and sesame seeds. Cool and refrigerate leftovers promptly; cooked rice must not remain lukewarm for hours.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-003.ingredient.0": "short-grain white rice",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-003.ingredient.1": "drinking water",
