    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-003.editorial.1": "COMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: once brand, SKU, products and official prices by store and format are available, verify ingredients, allergens and possible cross-contact against the actual label. Price alone does not certify food safety.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-004.title": "Tomato toast with olive oil (pan con tomate)",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-004.allergen": "CONTAINS WHEAT/GLUTEN. Check commercial bread for other allergens or traces. Garlic is optional and must be removed from the basket when deselected. Wash tomatoes and serve immediately; do not store assembled wet toast.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: once brand, SKU, products and official prices by store and format are available, verify ingredients, allergens and possible cross-contact against the actual label. Price alone does not certify food safety.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-004.step.0": "Wash and dry the tomatoes. Cut in half and grate the cut faces into a bowl, discarding the skin left in your hand.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-004.step.1": "Drain the grated tomato in a sieve for one minute if excessively watery; do not remove all the juice.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-004.step.2": "Cut 160 g of bread into two or four thick slices, approximately 80 g per person.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-004.step.3": "Toast in a toaster or clean frying pan for 2 minutes on each side, depending on thickness, until golden but not burnt.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-004.step.4": "If desired, rub the still-warm toast very lightly with the peeled garlic clove; leave it out if not wanted.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-004.step.5": "Divide the fresh tomato between the slices, add 10 ml of extra-virgin olive oil per serving and distribute the measured salt.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-004.step.6": "Serve immediately to preserve the contrast between crisp crust and juicy tomato. Do not store assembled toast for the next day.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-004.ingredient.0": "sliced sourdough wheat bread",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-004.ingredient.1": "ripe tomatoes",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-004.ingredient.2": "extra-virgin olive oil",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-004.ingredient.3": "fresh garlic, optional (clove)",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-004.ingredientNote.3": "Optional.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-004.ingredient.4": "salt",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-004.editorial.0": "CONTAINS WHEAT/GLUTEN. Check commercial bread for other allergens or traces. Garlic is optional and must be removed from the basket when deselected. Wash tomatoes and serve immediately; do not store assembled wet toast.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-004.editorial.1": "COMMERCIAL LABEL CHECK PENDING: once brand, SKU, products and official prices by store and format are available, verify ingredients, allergens and possible cross-contact against the actual label. Price alone does not certify food safety.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-005.title": "French toast with Canary Island banana and cinnamon",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-005.allergen": "CONTAINS WHEAT/GLUTEN, MILK AND EGG. Cook soaked bread until no liquid egg remains in the centre; keep raw egg mixture away from ready-to-eat foods. Discard unused raw mixture. Never give honey to babies under 12 months.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABELS PENDING: once the brand, SKU, product and official price for each store and store format are available, check ingredients, allergens and possible traces on the actual label. Price does not certify allergens.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-005.step.0": "Cut the day-old bread into four 2 cm-thick slices. If it is still too fresh, let it air out first so it holds together when soaked.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-005.step.1": "In a wide bowl, whisk both eggs with the milk, cinnamon and vanilla until evenly combined with no unmixed egg white.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-005.step.2": "Peel both bananas and slice them diagonally. Set them aside, but do not cut them too far in advance.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-005.step.3": "Heat a non-stick frying pan over medium heat and add half the butter.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-005.step.4": "Dip each bread slice into the mixture for 10–15 seconds per side: it should soak up the liquid but keep its shape.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-005.step.5": "Brown two slices at a time for about 2–3 minutes per side, until golden and cooked through with no runny egg in the centre. Repeat with the remaining butter and bread.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-005.step.6": "Divide the toast between two plates. Add one banana per serving, 10 g of honey and an extra pinch of cinnamon if desired.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-005.step.7": "Serve hot. Discard any leftover raw egg-and-milk mixture rather than saving it for use without cooking. Do not give honey to children under 12 months.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-005.ingredient.0": "day-old wheat bread",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-005.ingredient.1": "whole or semi-skimmed milk",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-005.ingredient.2": "fresh eggs",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-005.ingredient.3": "butter",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-005.ingredient.4": "ripe Canary Island bananas",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-005.ingredient.5": "honey",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-005.ingredient.6": "ground cinnamon",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-005.ingredient.7": "labelled vanilla extract",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-005.editorial.0": "CONTAINS WHEAT/GLUTEN, MILK AND EGG. Cook soaked bread until no liquid egg remains in the centre; keep raw egg mixture away from ready-to-eat foods. Discard unused raw mixture. Never give honey to babies under 12 months.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E12-BRK-005.editorial.1": "COMMERCIAL LABELS PENDING: once the brand, SKU, product and official price for each store and store format are available, check ingredients, allergens and possible traces on the actual label. Price does not certify allergens.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-R001.title": "Canary potatoes with mild green mojo and tomato",
    "recipesV83.JJ-R001.allergen": "No EU top-14 allergen is directly identified from the listed simple ingredients. Vinegar may contain sulphites depending on its label and the final concentration. Wash potatoes, coriander and tomato thoroughly; use drinking water for the mojo.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABELS PENDING: once the brand, SKU, product and official price for each store and store format are available, check ingredients, allergens and possible traces on the actual label. Price does not certify allergens.",
