    "recipesV83.JJ-R029.ingredient.6": "pure sweet paprika",
    "recipesV83.JJ-R029.editorial.0": "No EU-declarable allergens were identified in the listed simple ingredients; check labels and traces. Chill pork, avoid cross-contamination and check safe doneness with a thermometer; for a whole cut, use 63 °C and a 3-minute rest as a reference. Also check the sweet potato is tender.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-R029.editorial.1": "COMMERCIAL LABELS PENDING: once brand, SKU, product, actual label and official price per retailer and store format are available, check ingredients, allergens and precautionary traces. Price alone does not certify allergen status.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-R030.title": "Vieja (Canarian parrotfish) fillets en papillote with tomato and lemon",
    "recipesV83.JJ-R030.allergen": "Allergens identified from the declared ingredients: fish.\n\nFish bones and steam burns when opening the parcels; cook fish thoroughly and keep it refrigerated.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL PENDING: verify brand, SKU, ingredients, allergens and traces on the actual label when the official product and price are available for each store and store format. Price does not prove the absence of allergens.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-R030.step.0": "Preheat the oven to 190 °C. Carefully check the fish for remaining bones.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-R030.step.1": "Finely slice the onion and tomato and divide them between two parcels made from oven-safe baking parchment.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-R030.step.2": "Place one fillet on each parcel and season with oil, lemon and parsley. Close the paper loosely.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-R030.step.3": "Bake for 15 to 20 minutes, depending on thickness, until the fish is opaque and safely cooked; open the parcels carefully to avoid the steam.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-R030.ingredient.0": "boneless vieja (Canarian parrotfish) fillets",
    "recipesV83.JJ-R030.ingredient.1": "tomato",
    "recipesV83.JJ-R030.ingredient.2": "onion",
