    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-233.ingredient.15": "sunflower oil",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-233.ingredient.16": "salt",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.title": "Sichuan dan dan noodles with minced pork",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.allergen": "Allergens identifiable from the declared ingredients: wheat (gluten), soy, sesame, peanuts, mustard.\n\nYa cai comes from Chinese mustard greens: treat MUSTARD as a risk and check the package before serving anyone with mustard allergy. Wheat, soy, sesame and peanuts also feature; cook minced pork to 71 °C.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL PENDING: when official products and prices are available by supermarket and store format, verify BRAND, SKU, ACTUAL LABEL, ingredients, allergens and traces. Price does NOT establish safety or absence of allergens.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.step.0": "Mix the sesame paste, soy sauce, vinegar, sugar and chilli oil; loosen with some hot water until it forms a pourable sauce.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.step.1": "Heat the sunflower oil and stir-fry the minced pork for 6–8 minutes, breaking it into crumbs, until thoroughly cooked.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.step.2": "Add the chopped garlic and ginger, Sichuan pepper and ya cai; cook for another 2 minutes.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.step.3": "Boil the wheat noodles according to the packet and reserve a glass of cooking water.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.step.4": "Divide the sesame sauce between four bowls, add a little hot noodle water and stir to prevent it becoming too thick.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.step.5": "Place the hot noodles on top, then add the pork, chopped spring onion and roasted peanuts.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.step.6": "Serve immediately, mixing each bowl before eating; add extra chilli oil only if desired.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.ingredient.0": "Chinese wheat noodles",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.ingredient.1": "minced pork",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.ingredient.2": "sesame paste",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.ingredient.3": "soy sauce containing wheat",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.ingredient.4": "chilli oil",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.ingredient.5": "rice vinegar",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.ingredient.6": "garlic (dientes)",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.ingredient.7": "fresh ginger",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.ingredient.8": "spring onion",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.ingredient.9": "pickled Chinese mustard greens (ya cai)",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.ingredient.10": "roasted peanuts",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.ingredient.11": "Sichuan peppercorns",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.ingredient.12": "sugar",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.ingredient.13": "hot noodle cooking water",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-261.ingredient.14": "sunflower oil",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-287.title": "Northern Thai chicken khao soi",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-287.allergen": "Allergens identifiable from the declared ingredients: wheat (gluten), egg, fish, mustard.\n\nDeclared ingredients include wheat, egg, fish and mustard greens. Curry paste may contain CRUSTACEANS even if its name does not say so; check labels. Cook chicken to 74 °C and take care with hot frying oil.\n\nCOMMERCIAL LABEL PENDING: when official products and prices are available by supermarket and store format, verify BRAND, SKU, ACTUAL LABEL, ingredients, allergens and traces. Price does NOT establish safety or absence of allergens.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-287.step.0": "Cut the chicken into medium pieces. Set aside 90 g of noodles for the crispy topping and keep the rest for boiling.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-287.step.1": "Heat 20 ml of the sunflower oil and fry the curry paste and yellow curry powder for 2 minutes over medium heat.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-287.step.2": "Add some of the thick coconut milk and stir to blend the spices; add the chicken, remaining coconut milk and stock.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-287.step.3": "Simmer for 25–30 minutes until the chicken is tender and reaches 74 °C; season with fish sauce and sugar.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-287.step.4": "Fry the reserved 90 g of noodles in hot oil in small batches until crisp; drain on paper.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-287.step.5": "Boil the remaining 340 g of noodles according to the package, drain and divide between four bowls.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-287.step.6": "Cover with the chicken and curry broth; finish with the crispy noodles, thinly sliced shallot, pickled greens, coriander and lime wedges.",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-287.ingredient.0": "skinless chicken thighs",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-287.ingredient.1": "wheat and egg noodles",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-287.ingredient.2": "coconut milk",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-287.ingredient.3": "chicken stock",
    "recipesV83.JJ-E13-287.ingredient.4": "red curry paste with no declared crustacean ingredient",
